# Compiler caches. Belt and braces: the scripts point these at out/ (already ignored),
# but a stray TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR or a new script must not be able to commit them.
.inductor_cache/
.triton_cache/
**/.inductor_cache/
**/.triton_cache/

# Small build artefacts that every box has to hold an IDENTICAL copy of, and that
# `*.pt` above would otherwise swallow. About 4.4 MB in total.
#   perms/           vocabulary permutations. A factorised head is fitted to one
#                    specific assignment, so a box without it silently trains the
#                    token-id control instead of the arm you asked for.
#   tokenizer*/      the tokenizers themselves. Rebuilding one is a BPE training run,
#                    and two boxes that rebuilt separately are not the same tokenizer.
# Directory negations come first: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, and tokenizer_131k/ is excluded by name above.
#
# tokenizer/ stays TRACKED on purpose. Untracking it would make `git pull` DELETE the
# tokenizer on every box whose copy is clean, or refuse the pull outright on a box whose
# copy differs. Tracked and pinned instead, a pull repairs a box that is on a bad copy.
# What it is pinned to lives in tokenizer/PINNED.json (V=32768) and
# tests/test_tokenizer_pin.py fails if the tracked files ever stop matching it.
#
# The failure this guards against: tokenizer.pkl flip-flopped between the real 412 KB
# V=32768 file and a 1.9 KB V=265 byte-level stub across five commits, because anything
# that writes into ./tokenizer gets swept into the next commit. A run against the stub
# does not fail. base_train prints "Vocab size: 265", pads to 320 and trains to
# completion, so a whole sweep can produce bpb numbers that compare with nothing.
!perms/
!perms/**
!tokenizer/
!tokenizer/**
!tokenizer_131k/
!tokenizer_131k/**

# Literature review papers
Literature Review/
[Ll]iterature [Rr]eview/
